1
00:00:09,280 --> 00:00:11,340
This is how I'll become.

2
00:00:13,980 --> 00:00:15,980
This is how I'll become.

3
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:19,840
Supreme Commander!

4
00:00:21,100 --> 00:00:22,037
A hero!

5
00:00:22,120 --> 00:00:23,800
This is my story!

6
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,060
In the dark, dark, and dark.

7
00:00:35,080 --> 00:00:37,617
One, one, one, one.

8
00:00:37,700 --> 00:00:38,900
In the shadows,

9
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:41,477
I'm trying to cry.

10
00:00:41,560 --> 00:00:43,937
The dream of my dream?

11
00:00:44,020 --> 00:00:45,537
Oh, oh, oh, oh,

12
00:00:45,620 --> 00:00:52,620
oh.

13
00:01:15,520 --> 00:01:21,200
I'll be back once again.
I'll never move forward.

14
00:01:21,440 --> 00:01:24,020
I'll never leave you alone.

15
00:01:28,320 --> 00:01:29,377
I'll never leave you alone.

16
00:01:29,460 --> 00:01:32,760
I'll be with you forever.

17
00:01:33,920 --> 00:01:36,660
I'll never let you change this world.

18
00:01:36,880 --> 00:01:37,710
I'll never change my life.

19
00:01:37,793 --> 00:01:38,880
I'll never be with you.

20
00:02:05,300 --> 00:02:07,180
Welcome, ma 'am. Thank you.

21
00:02:09,180 --> 00:02:11,420
Yuki, I'm going to do the paperwork.

22
00:02:11,820 --> 00:02:12,697
Wait for me outside.

23
00:02:12,780 --> 00:02:13,610
Uh, sure.

24
00:02:15,180 --> 00:02:19,220
So the 5th Squad's gateway is
connected all the way to Yamagata?

25
00:02:19,700 --> 00:02:22,417
It was only a 20-minute
drive on the other side.

26
00:02:22,500 --> 00:02:24,317
Interdimensional travel is nuts.

27
00:02:24,400 --> 00:02:25,518
Thanks for waiting.

28
00:02:32,820 --> 00:02:33,650
What's wrong?

29
00:02:35,180 --> 00:02:36,060
Oh, yeah!

30
00:02:36,340 --> 00:02:38,928
It's just nice to be
back in our home world.

31
00:02:39,840 --> 00:02:42,417
We'd all burn out without a break
from work every now and then.

32
00:02:42,500 --> 00:02:44,324
But time off's in short supply.

33
00:02:44,640 --> 00:02:46,517
Enjoy the fresh air while you can.

34
00:02:46,600 --> 00:02:47,430
Yeah.

35
00:02:50,020 --> 00:02:54,180
I never really noticed till
now, but she's really pretty.

36
00:02:55,520 --> 00:02:56,977
Look ahead when you walk.

37
00:02:57,060 --> 00:02:58,137
Oh, sorry about that.

38
00:02:58,220 --> 00:03:01,420
By the way, may I ask where we're going?

39
00:03:07,640 --> 00:03:08,470
Hmm?

40
00:03:10,240 --> 00:03:11,070
Yuki!

41
00:03:11,580 --> 00:03:12,640
Yuki! Yuki!

42
00:03:13,940 --> 00:03:15,280
Have you seen Yuki?

43
00:03:15,760 --> 00:03:18,997
Yeah, he went out with the
commander for some time off earlier.

44
00:03:19,080 --> 00:03:20,800
He did? Uh-huh.

45
00:03:21,300 --> 00:03:26,065
Himari took them to the Yamagata Passage
while she was out on her regular patrol.

46
00:03:27,800 --> 00:03:28,677
That's right.

47
00:03:28,760 --> 00:03:30,220
Today is...

48
00:03:33,940 --> 00:03:36,160
There was an incident at Mount Kasan,

49
00:03:36,440 --> 00:03:39,920
in Oisawa, where dozens of
Shuki wandered into this world.

50
00:03:40,420 --> 00:03:42,538
One of them was especially powerful.

51
00:03:42,860 --> 00:03:45,331
I remember it as though it were yesterday.

52
00:03:49,160 --> 00:03:52,617
It had a single horn that stuck
out from the top of its head.

53
00:03:52,700 --> 00:03:55,240
So I called it the Unihorn.

54
00:03:59,380 --> 00:04:02,377
All of the Shuki that crossed
over that day were wiped

55
00:04:02,460 --> 00:04:05,377
out by the demon defense
force who arrived to help.

56
00:04:05,460 --> 00:04:06,477
Or so I thought.

57
00:04:06,560 --> 00:04:09,020
But after looking through the records,

58
00:04:09,460 --> 00:04:13,877
I discovered the Unihorn managed to
escape back through the gateway into Mato.

59
00:04:13,960 --> 00:04:16,020
So then the Unihorn is still alive.

60
00:04:16,600 --> 00:04:19,700
I have a score to settle
with that damn Shuki.

61
00:04:20,480 --> 00:04:23,580
I swear, I will destroy that thing.

62
00:04:23,840 --> 00:04:27,016
And I want you to be prepared
for when that day comes.

63
00:04:27,680 --> 00:04:30,327
That's what I brought
you here to talk about.

64
00:04:30,660 --> 00:04:33,380
I will avenge everyone who died.

65
00:04:42,700 --> 00:04:44,818
It's time for us to go back to Mato.

66
00:04:44,940 --> 00:04:46,528
Wait a minute, Miss Kyouka.

67
00:04:46,980 --> 00:04:48,509
Can we take a break first?

68
00:04:48,700 --> 00:04:50,112
I did a little research.

69
00:04:50,260 --> 00:04:52,520
This cafe is famous for its parfaits.

70
00:04:52,900 --> 00:04:55,560
Mato is far more important. Check it out!

71
00:04:56,120 --> 00:04:57,020
Look at that!

72
00:04:57,340 --> 00:04:58,693
It's amazing, isn't it?

73
00:05:00,780 --> 00:05:02,192
Fine, but make it short.

74
00:05:04,620 --> 00:05:06,797
You're more assertive than
I thought you would be.

75
00:05:06,880 --> 00:05:08,257
You surprise me.

76
00:05:08,340 --> 00:05:11,537
Well, you enjoy sweet treats
like everyone else, don't you?

77
00:05:11,620 --> 00:05:14,637
I'm just more concerned about
motto than I am about desserts.

78
00:05:14,720 --> 00:05:20,097
I lost my big sister in a motto mishap a
while ago, so it's important to me too.

79
00:05:20,180 --> 00:05:21,440
I totally get it.

80
00:05:23,700 --> 00:05:28,053
But you'll miss your chance at vengeance
if you run yourself ragged first.

81
00:05:28,980 --> 00:05:31,333
We'd burn out without a break from work.

82
00:05:31,740 --> 00:05:32,570
Remember?

83
00:05:33,200 --> 00:05:37,680
Persuasion is another forte of yours,
I see. Very nice. Here you are.

84
00:05:38,820 --> 00:05:41,360
Let's see how good this parfait really is.

85
00:05:44,780 --> 00:05:46,300
Wow, fantastic!

86
00:05:48,780 --> 00:05:49,660
What's wrong?

87
00:05:50,440 --> 00:05:51,270
Nothing.

88
00:05:51,380 --> 00:05:53,145
Just caught up in my thoughts.

89
00:05:56,440 --> 00:05:57,270
Delish.

90
00:05:57,540 --> 00:05:59,837
Seeing a smile on Kyoka's
face for the first

91
00:05:59,920 --> 00:06:03,220
time actually brought back
memories of my sister.

92
00:06:03,700 --> 00:06:05,120
Wow, it's delicious.

93
00:06:05,640 --> 00:06:09,897
I took your suggestion from yesterday
and added a little bit of Yuzu citrus.

94
00:06:09,980 --> 00:06:13,297
You're such a smart little cookie,
I give it a million thumbs up.

95
00:06:13,380 --> 00:06:14,556
I'm so proud of you.

96
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:18,471
Keep up all of your hard work, okay, Yuki?

97
00:06:18,800 --> 00:06:21,624
Boys are defined by their
skills in the kitchen.

98
00:06:24,500 --> 00:06:25,637
Are you going to have any?

99
00:06:25,720 --> 00:06:29,200
Oh, um, um, it's delicious.

100
00:06:29,580 --> 00:06:32,217
The parfaits here really
are as good as they say.

101
00:06:32,300 --> 00:06:33,130
Yeah.

102
00:06:34,920 --> 00:06:36,060
A conch shell?

103
00:06:36,320 --> 00:06:38,261
It's an emergency call from Mato.

104
00:06:38,520 --> 00:06:41,117
A single blow of the shell
means it's not life-threatening.

105
00:06:41,200 --> 00:06:43,965
But something serious is
happening nonetheless.

106
00:06:45,180 --> 00:06:46,380
Break time is over.

107
00:06:46,820 --> 00:06:48,220
We need to hurry back.

108
00:06:49,160 --> 00:06:50,480
You want that here?

109
00:06:52,420 --> 00:06:53,280
Oh, wow.

110
00:07:05,200 --> 00:07:06,520
That wiped me out.

111
00:07:06,740 --> 00:07:08,777
We made it back home in no time flat.

112
00:07:08,860 --> 00:07:09,690
Nicely done.

113
00:07:09,800 --> 00:07:11,097
I'm going to go change.

114
00:07:11,180 --> 00:07:12,010
Okay.

115
00:07:15,840 --> 00:07:18,220
Why don't you come with me? Huh?

116
00:07:22,940 --> 00:07:23,940
So, um...

117
00:07:25,020 --> 00:07:27,079
Start by helping me take these off.

118
00:07:28,460 --> 00:07:30,920
Um, is this my reward from your ability?

119
00:07:31,260 --> 00:07:33,357
And what the hell else
could it possibly be?

120
00:07:33,440 --> 00:07:35,146
Oh yeah, that's a good point.

121
00:07:35,840 --> 00:07:37,400
Hurry up. Yes, ma 'am.

122
00:07:38,880 --> 00:07:41,640
Holy crap, we're deep in fetish territory.

123
00:07:42,120 --> 00:07:45,944
Does that mean I'm wishing for
this kind of stuff subconsciously?

124
00:07:47,900 --> 00:07:49,547
It's exactly what you think.

125
00:07:57,480 --> 00:07:58,980
You damn pervert.

126
00:08:00,760 --> 00:08:02,054
Welcome back, you two.

127
00:08:02,660 --> 00:08:03,954
Give me the breakdown.

128
00:08:04,220 --> 00:08:06,977
There was a discovery made
during today's patrols.

129
00:08:07,060 --> 00:08:10,942
A crater-like formation appeared
about 21 kilometers to the south,

130
00:08:11,120 --> 00:08:13,037
along with a large number of Shuki.

131
00:08:13,120 --> 00:08:13,950
Hold on.

132
00:08:14,033 --> 00:08:15,957
Are all of those red dots
supposed to be Shuki?

133
00:08:16,040 --> 00:08:17,060
A crater, huh?

134
00:08:17,300 --> 00:08:19,297
We've never seen anything like that.

135
00:08:19,380 --> 00:08:22,057
They're not making any moves
to leave that area either.

136
00:08:22,140 --> 00:08:24,740
It's like a nest of some kind, right?

137
00:08:25,560 --> 00:08:27,617
Apologies for ruining your day off.

138
00:08:27,700 --> 00:08:28,530
That's okay.

139
00:08:28,613 --> 00:08:29,443
Good work.

140
00:08:29,526 --> 00:08:31,322
This problem needs our attention

141
00:08:31,820 --> 00:08:34,720
This is a huge undertaking
for the seventh squad.

142
00:08:35,020 --> 00:08:37,320
Yeah, let's smash them all like bugs

143
00:08:38,300 --> 00:08:39,380
Someone's fired up

144
00:08:40,600 --> 00:08:41,800
Prepare to move out.

145
00:08:42,140 --> 00:08:43,787
We'll ride in three vehicles

146
00:08:44,200 --> 00:08:45,030
Right!

147
00:08:48,840 --> 00:08:50,740
I count as the third vehicle?

148
00:08:51,180 --> 00:08:53,060
We're going on ahead. Yuki!

149
00:08:58,340 --> 00:08:59,480
He's fast.

150
00:08:59,920 --> 00:09:01,700
He's just a wild animal.

151
00:09:05,660 --> 00:09:08,601
It would be horrific if
any people got stuck here.

152
00:09:08,740 --> 00:09:09,975
Let's clear them out.

153
00:09:10,080 --> 00:09:11,000
Don't rush it.

154
00:09:11,260 --> 00:09:12,907
You will wait for my signal.

155
00:09:13,180 --> 00:09:17,474
It'll take the seventh squad's perfect
teamwork to eliminate all of them.

156
00:09:20,320 --> 00:09:21,460
Here it goes!

157
00:09:23,340 --> 00:09:24,660
Kimari! I'm on it!

158
00:09:29,320 --> 00:09:32,697
If they merge, it'll be easier
than taking them down one by one.

159
00:09:32,780 --> 00:09:34,117
That's our time to shine.

160
00:09:34,200 --> 00:09:36,277
We'll crush the big one and call it a day.

161
00:09:36,360 --> 00:09:39,977
The Shuki are tough bastards, but
their fighting style is simplistic.

162
00:09:40,060 --> 00:09:41,397
Our strategy is flawless.

163
00:09:41,480 --> 00:09:45,200
Once they've reshaped, we will
destroy them once and for all.

164
00:09:45,540 --> 00:09:47,837
Be ready to jump into battle at any time.

165
00:09:47,920 --> 00:09:48,750
Yes, ma 'am!

166
00:09:49,080 --> 00:09:50,920
Huh? It's Kyoka!

167
00:09:51,460 --> 00:09:52,290
Shushu!

168
00:09:57,680 --> 00:09:58,510
Shushu!

169
00:10:02,840 --> 00:10:05,680
One horn on top of its head!

170
00:10:07,280 --> 00:10:08,340
It's him.

171
00:10:12,780 --> 00:10:13,660
Damn it!

172
00:10:21,180 --> 00:10:24,140
I'm here to join the party. It talks?

173
00:10:24,420 --> 00:10:26,360
Are you some kind of monster?

174
00:10:26,600 --> 00:10:29,100
Now that's not a very nice thing to say.

175
00:10:29,400 --> 00:10:30,360
Be careful.

176
00:10:30,880 --> 00:10:33,233
Because I have more than a sharp tongue!

177
00:10:38,040 --> 00:10:38,870
Himity!

178
00:10:46,800 --> 00:10:48,640
Ah, that felt great!

179
00:10:53,060 --> 00:10:55,800
Well now, aren't we a tough one?

180
00:10:56,040 --> 00:10:57,600
I finally found it.

181
00:10:57,780 --> 00:10:59,500
That unicorn will die!

182
00:10:59,840 --> 00:11:03,428
Huh, it sounds like they have
a cute little nickname for you.

183
00:11:03,660 --> 00:11:06,895
That's him, the bastard who
destroyed Kyoka's hometown.

184
00:11:10,760 --> 00:11:12,340
You! On the Shuki!

185
00:11:12,700 --> 00:11:13,780
Who are you?

186
00:11:14,040 --> 00:11:18,160
I guess you could say I'm the
Demon Defense Force's archenemy.

187
00:11:18,960 --> 00:11:20,020
Amato Peach?

188
00:11:20,320 --> 00:11:23,540
By the way, have you seen
my little brother anywhere?

189
00:11:24,680 --> 00:11:25,900
Easy to spot.

190
00:11:26,340 --> 00:11:29,340
I mean, seeing as he's
incredibly handsome.

191
00:11:35,080 --> 00:11:38,420
Little brother there are
more of these things.

192
00:11:50,580 --> 00:11:52,877
My little brother was
obsessed with me when

193
00:11:52,960 --> 00:11:55,357
we were younger always
following me around.

194
00:11:55,440 --> 00:11:57,280
Annoying, but adorable!

195
00:11:58,880 --> 00:12:03,700
In spite of that, the instant he got
older, he turned into such a rabble!

196
00:12:04,520 --> 00:12:08,777
But those were the fun days, because
I got to knock some manners into him!

197
00:12:08,860 --> 00:12:09,860
It can talk?

198
00:12:10,120 --> 00:12:12,180
Is it a Shuki? Whatever.

199
00:12:12,540 --> 00:12:15,897
All that matters right now is that this
one's clearly different from the rest.

200
00:12:15,980 --> 00:12:17,745
My little brother's name is...

201
00:12:26,300 --> 00:12:29,380
I'm talking about my brothers!

202
00:12:30,060 --> 00:12:31,820
So don't get to wrap me!

203
00:12:34,380 --> 00:12:35,540
Have a snack.

204
00:12:38,780 --> 00:12:40,040
I get it.

205
00:12:40,380 --> 00:12:42,720
You must be their supreme commander!

206
00:12:43,180 --> 00:12:44,320
My goodness!

207
00:12:44,700 --> 00:12:47,229
You don't know anything
about Mato, do you?

208
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:55,240
This is a world filled with curses!

209
00:12:59,140 --> 00:12:59,970
Help!

210
00:13:00,680 --> 00:13:04,562
You've got a nice shuki of your
own, but it's time to say goodbye!

211
00:13:13,380 --> 00:13:14,210
Huh?

212
00:13:18,420 --> 00:13:20,600
This isn't Ashuki. You're...

213
00:13:34,340 --> 00:13:35,540
You coward!

214
00:13:35,820 --> 00:13:38,420
Don't run away from me! Miss Kyoka!

215
00:13:39,060 --> 00:13:39,980
Fine, then.

216
00:13:40,240 --> 00:13:43,337
I'll do exactly what you did
to all those fleeing villagers!

217
00:13:43,420 --> 00:13:44,880
And tear you to pieces!

218
00:13:45,480 --> 00:13:46,360
Yuki, now!

219
00:13:46,600 --> 00:13:47,718
What are you doing?

220
00:13:47,820 --> 00:13:49,055
They're getting away!

221
00:13:53,260 --> 00:13:54,560
Shushu, are you okay?

222
00:13:54,780 --> 00:13:55,740
Yeah, I'm fine.

223
00:14:01,280 --> 00:14:02,400
Yuki! Huh?

224
00:14:03,860 --> 00:14:06,097
Heimari and Shushu, safety is priority.

225
00:14:06,180 --> 00:14:07,537
We're gonna pull back now.

226
00:14:07,620 --> 00:14:08,450
Yes, ma 'am!

227
00:14:09,720 --> 00:14:10,960
What was I thinking?

228
00:14:11,420 --> 00:14:13,297
I let my rage take over.

229
00:14:13,380 --> 00:14:16,140
and it almost cost me my squad mates.

230
00:14:24,420 --> 00:14:27,017
Fortunately, their wounds
are relatively minor.

231
00:14:27,100 --> 00:14:28,917
They'll be fully recovered by tomorrow.

232
00:14:29,000 --> 00:14:30,060
That's great news!

233
00:14:33,840 --> 00:14:34,670
Anyway,

234
00:14:34,753 --> 00:14:39,028
I can't believe the kind of filthy rewards
that come out of your subconscious.

235
00:14:40,420 --> 00:14:42,257
Seriously, what is wrong with you?

236
00:14:42,340 --> 00:14:43,399
You're disgusting.

237
00:14:44,060 --> 00:14:44,890
Yeah, I know.

238
00:14:45,380 --> 00:14:49,086
The demands of my inner psyche
are starting to terrify me, too.

239
00:14:50,320 --> 00:14:52,144
In regards to that last battle,

240
00:14:52,320 --> 00:14:55,057
I have a lot of questions and
comments to go over with you.

241
00:14:55,140 --> 00:14:56,057
For starters...

242
00:14:56,140 --> 00:14:58,517
I have something I want
to report to you as well.

243
00:14:58,600 --> 00:15:00,437
But does it have to be
while we're like this?

244
00:15:00,520 --> 00:15:02,120
I don't want to waste time.

245
00:15:02,260 --> 00:15:05,613
And this reward of yours isn't
going to end anytime soon.

246
00:15:06,120 --> 00:15:08,649
I'm really sorry that
the Unihorn got away.

247
00:15:09,100 --> 00:15:11,657
Shushu's and Himari's
lives were more important.

248
00:15:11,740 --> 00:15:14,093
I appreciate all that you did out there.

249
00:15:15,200 --> 00:15:19,140
Well, you have an interesting
way of showing it. Shut up!

250
00:15:19,320 --> 00:15:23,202
This is something that you
subconsciously asked for, you perverse!

251
00:15:29,220 --> 00:15:30,540
Back to the Unihorn.

252
00:15:30,820 --> 00:15:34,840
That humanoid writing on top of
it must be some species of Shuki.

253
00:15:35,180 --> 00:15:38,117
It's crazy to think that a
Shuki could speak our language.

254
00:15:38,200 --> 00:15:40,965
This news is going to
shock the entire country.

255
00:15:42,020 --> 00:15:44,140
Well, speaking of that new species,

256
00:15:44,420 --> 00:15:47,680
remember when I told you
about my missing big sister?

257
00:15:48,340 --> 00:15:50,760
I think that thing kind of resembled her.

258
00:15:50,960 --> 00:15:53,800
So you're saying it might
be your sister? Maybe.

259
00:15:54,180 --> 00:15:56,740
It was just a feeling I had.

260
00:15:57,320 --> 00:16:01,420
But also, it had a strange
reaction when it saw my face.

261
00:16:02,100 --> 00:16:02,930
Hmm.

262
00:16:03,520 --> 00:16:06,877
Well, it did say something about
searching for a little brother.

263
00:16:06,960 --> 00:16:10,254
I'm betting that just triggered
memories of your sister.

264
00:16:14,140 --> 00:16:18,728
Besides, it told us that its brother is
supposedly the most handsome man ever.

265
00:16:19,020 --> 00:16:20,500
And, well...

266
00:16:21,780 --> 00:16:22,760
Yeah, true.

267
00:16:22,960 --> 00:16:24,397
That doesn't describe me at all.

268
00:16:24,480 --> 00:16:25,797
It was a ridiculous thought.

269
00:16:25,880 --> 00:16:29,233
In any case, no ordinary human
could ever be that strong.

270
00:16:29,440 --> 00:16:33,800
In addition, nobody's ever heard
of a human becoming a Shuki before.

271
00:16:36,320 --> 00:16:38,897
We're most certainly bound
to cross paths again.

272
00:16:38,980 --> 00:16:42,620
because we won't stop looking
until we find them. Right.

273
00:16:44,020 --> 00:16:47,373
It's weird how excited you
seem about getting stepped on.

274
00:16:47,720 --> 00:16:50,240
I mean, the view is nice from down here.

275
00:16:51,700 --> 00:16:53,180
God damn it.

276
00:16:54,080 --> 00:16:55,620
Miss Kyoka? No way!

277
00:16:59,120 --> 00:17:03,117
Miss Kyoka seemed convinced that
it was a humanoid species of Shuki.

278
00:17:03,200 --> 00:17:07,997
But if it really was my sister, why would
she be attacking the demon defense forces?

279
00:17:08,080 --> 00:17:10,580
How has she stayed alive all this time?

280
00:17:10,800 --> 00:17:13,780
And why is she working
with that horn monstrosity?

281
00:17:14,020 --> 00:17:15,457
If we see them again, what should I...

282
00:17:15,540 --> 00:17:17,520
Oh no! Mr. Yuki! Mr. Yuki!

283
00:17:17,820 --> 00:17:19,585
Look, the pot is boiling over!

284
00:17:20,780 --> 00:17:21,610
Ah!

285
00:17:21,693 --> 00:17:22,900
I'm sorry, I was spacing out!

286
00:17:23,420 --> 00:17:24,817
Kneel down here, please,

287
00:17:24,900 --> 00:17:28,517
as your senpai Nei needs to take
care of some serious business!

288
00:17:28,600 --> 00:17:30,200
What does she mean by that?

289
00:17:31,060 --> 00:17:34,037
You expose this to danger,
and you must be punished!

290
00:17:34,120 --> 00:17:35,037
Senpai, punch!

291
00:17:35,120 --> 00:17:36,060
I'm sorry!

292
00:17:37,560 --> 00:17:42,057
You had a big day out there fighting those
tough enemies to save Shushu from danger?

293
00:17:42,140 --> 00:17:45,297
You're tired and your body
and brain need a rest.

294
00:17:45,380 --> 00:17:48,377
I'm not the best cook, but
I can make simple meals.

295
00:17:48,460 --> 00:17:50,519
Would you like me to handle dinner?

296
00:17:50,740 --> 00:17:51,980
Wow, thank you.

297
00:17:52,640 --> 00:17:54,677
It's all part of being a good senpai!

298
00:17:54,760 --> 00:17:56,097
But I can't do it.

299
00:17:56,180 --> 00:17:57,320
I'm good to cook.

300
00:17:58,080 --> 00:18:00,377
I don't deserve such an amazing senpai.

301
00:18:00,460 --> 00:18:01,520
Thank you.

302
00:18:04,680 --> 00:18:08,617
Now, I would however take your help
plating the food, would you mind?

303
00:18:08,700 --> 00:18:10,360
Just leave it out of me!

304
00:18:10,860 --> 00:18:14,837
I can figure out whether she's my
sister or not the next time we meet.

305
00:18:14,920 --> 00:18:17,180
For now, I gotta focus on work.

306
00:18:18,160 --> 00:18:20,980
Crawling back here with injuries, really.

307
00:18:21,520 --> 00:18:25,300
And I thought you were
above such disgraces, Alba.

308
00:18:26,460 --> 00:18:27,660
What can I say?

309
00:18:27,920 --> 00:18:29,840
I got taken by surprise.

310
00:18:31,200 --> 00:18:32,318
They're all better.

311
00:18:33,260 --> 00:18:34,380
It's perfect!

312
00:18:35,540 --> 00:18:36,760
Thank you, Coco.

313
00:18:38,440 --> 00:18:39,270
Hey!

314
00:18:40,720 --> 00:18:43,100
That was Yuki, I'm sure of it.

315
00:18:44,180 --> 00:18:46,617
But I don't know why
he looked like a Shuki?

316
00:18:46,700 --> 00:18:49,140
An experiment by the demon defense force?

317
00:18:49,420 --> 00:18:51,773
Or the ability of that woman riding him?

318
00:18:52,140 --> 00:18:55,375
When did they start letting
guys in their organization?

319
00:18:55,700 --> 00:18:57,560
But it was a nice reunion

320
00:18:58,380 --> 00:18:59,210
Right?

321
00:18:59,293 --> 00:19:04,997
Yuki the unicorn was crazy powerful if we

322
00:19:05,080 --> 00:19:11,017
fight again you're already back in action.

323
00:19:11,100 --> 00:19:15,537
Yep tip-top shape and thank you for
saving me when I was in trouble.

324
00:19:15,620 --> 00:19:17,740
Of course don't mention it.

325
00:19:20,840 --> 00:19:25,120
Why don't I let you return the
favor with a nice little back scrub?

326
00:19:25,460 --> 00:19:27,457
Hey, enough with the jokes already!

327
00:19:27,540 --> 00:19:29,481
You sure you want to turn around?

328
00:19:30,020 --> 00:19:32,200
Because I'm completely naked.

329
00:19:33,240 --> 00:19:36,200
So just quiet down and
let me wash your back.

330
00:19:39,540 --> 00:19:41,800
Okay, big guy, here we go.

331
00:19:43,680 --> 00:19:45,637
Is she actually naked back there?

332
00:19:45,720 --> 00:19:48,249
I can't risk turning
around if that's true.

333
00:19:48,960 --> 00:19:50,677
Shushu's pulling this
little prank because she

334
00:19:50,760 --> 00:19:53,257
thinks I'm not the type of
guy who would turn around.

335
00:19:53,340 --> 00:19:56,057
Or maybe that's just what
she wants me to think.

336
00:19:56,140 --> 00:19:58,317
I hear that most people are
prone to playing it safe,

337
00:19:58,400 --> 00:20:00,757
so confidently turning around and saying,

338
00:20:00,840 --> 00:20:03,557
I knew you had a swimsuit
on, now get out of here,

339
00:20:03,640 --> 00:20:06,477
would be the smart move in
order to teach her a lesson.

340
00:20:06,560 --> 00:20:07,390
Here goes!

341
00:20:07,620 --> 00:20:09,640
I wasn't bored yesterday, Shushu!

342
00:20:12,820 --> 00:20:13,650
Ah!

343
00:20:14,180 --> 00:20:15,010
Warm the air!

344
00:20:15,180 --> 00:20:16,356
Away from me, woman!

345
00:20:17,680 --> 00:20:19,680
Yuki just saw me naked!

346
00:20:20,040 --> 00:20:21,640
Now my heart's racing!

347
00:20:23,880 --> 00:20:24,710
Huh?

348
00:20:31,720 --> 00:20:33,537
I guess you're ready to find me!

349
00:20:33,620 --> 00:20:34,502
I'm interested!

350
00:20:37,000 --> 00:20:37,940
Hold on!

351
00:20:40,120 --> 00:20:42,520
I put up a sign that said Bath Occupied!

352
00:20:42,680 --> 00:20:45,209
Well, you should have
made it more clear...

353
00:20:45,640 --> 00:20:48,758
that it was a guy in the
bath, you perverted asshole!

354
00:20:56,440 --> 00:20:57,800
Well, hello there.

355
00:21:00,180 --> 00:21:02,709
Never a dull moment
with the seventh squad.

356
00:21:03,660 --> 00:21:04,542
Intruder alert!

357
00:21:04,800 --> 00:21:06,617
They're members of the sixth squad.

358
00:21:06,700 --> 00:21:07,530
Oh.

359
00:21:07,800 --> 00:21:10,660
I'm the commander, Miss Tenka Izumo.

360
00:21:14,580 --> 00:21:17,300
I'm her second-in-command, Yachiho Azuma.

361
00:21:19,940 --> 00:21:20,770
Azuma?

362
00:21:22,820 --> 00:21:25,600
So you're the slave I've
heard so much about.

363
00:21:28,720 --> 00:21:31,320
Well, anyway, go fetch Kyo for me.

364
00:21:31,820 --> 00:21:33,291
Uh, you mean Miss Kyouka?

365
00:21:33,600 --> 00:21:34,760
Sure, right away!

366
00:22:17,740 --> 00:22:20,540
Thank you.

367
00:23:10,100 --> 00:23:12,460
T-Chat Maze Empire! Okay!

368
00:23:12,800 --> 00:23:16,997
Today we're going to talk about my Peach
ability called Share Defined Promises.

369
00:23:17,080 --> 00:23:20,437
Known as Clairvoyance, this
allows me to see places far away,

370
00:23:20,520 --> 00:23:22,817
which I used to find
Shuki and Mato victims.

371
00:23:22,900 --> 00:23:26,077
I can also share the POV of a
person who's touched me before.

372
00:23:26,160 --> 00:23:27,925
It's valued by scouting teams.

373
00:23:28,140 --> 00:23:29,617
There are some places I can't see,

374
00:23:29,700 --> 00:23:32,237
like inside caves, and it's
pretty useless in combat.

375
00:23:32,320 --> 00:23:35,337
But I believe that I have my own
role to play and always give my best.
